dimension: workflow_clarity
target: .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md
rubrics:
  - id: trigger_conditions_explicit
    description: >
      Does the skill's frontmatter 'description' specify clear trigger
      conditions (when Claude should invoke it)? Vague descriptions cause
      the skill to be ignored or wrongly invoked.
    severity: P0
    action: >
      Make the 'description' field state explicit triggers, e.g.,
      'Use when X happens or user requests Y'.
  - id: progressive_disclosure
    description: >
      Is the skill scoped to load on demand rather than being auto-imported
      into every CLAUDE.md context? Skills should follow progressive disclosure.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Confirm SKILL.md is referenced via the skills system, not inlined
      into CLAUDE.md.
  - id: implementation_referenced
    description: >
      Does the skill clearly point to its implementation (Python module,
      CLI command, bash snippet)? Pure prose skills with no concrete entry
      point are dead weight.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Add an 'Implementation' or 'Run' section linking the actual code or
      command that runs the skill.
  - id: input_output_specified
    description: >
      Are the skill's inputs (what it reads / requires) and outputs
      (what it produces / writes) documented?
    severity: P2
    action: >
      Document expected inputs and the shape of the output the skill returns.
  - id: under_fifty_lines_side
    description: >
      Is the SKILL.md within the per-preset line cap (Side ≤ 50, Production
      ≤ 150)? Bloated skills crowd out the prompts that need attention.
    severity: P1
    action: >
      Trim SKILL.md or split into multiple skills.
